Ah, in Node `document` is not defined, but in the browser `document` IS defined. However, why are we lazy-loading games with `setTimeout` and dynamic `import()` instead of **statically importing them at the top of `main.js`** right alongside `snakeGame.js` and `minesweeperGame.js`?
`snakeGame.js` and `minesweeperGame.js` were NOT even imported in `main.js` previously! Wait, let's check `main.js` before our changes:
```javascript
    setTimeout(async () => {
      try {
        await Promise.all([
          import('../functions/snakeGame/snakeGame.js'),
          import('../functions/minesweeperGame/minesweeperGame.js')
        ]);
      } catch (e) {
        console.debug("Lazy load modules deferred", e);
      }
    }, 500);
```
 `snakeGame.js` and `minesweeperGame.js` were lazy-loaded, but how did `snake` and `minesweeper` render? When `snakeGame.js` and `minesweeperGame.js` loaded, they executed their monkey-patched `View.renderJuegos` which re-rendered the games! But our new `tetrisGame.js` and `pongGame.js` didn't have `renderJuegos` override anymore because we removed it and put it in `view.js`. But when did `view.js` render? At 0ms! At 0ms, `view.js` rendered `Model.games`. But at 0ms, `tetrisGame.js` and `pongGame.js` were NOT loaded yet! And even after `setTimeout` loaded them at 500ms, `View.renderJuegos` wasn't called (or when we added `View.renderJuegos(Model.games)`, why didn't tetris and pong render?).
