LOOK AT THAT ERROR!
`ReferenceError: document is not defined at file:///C:/Users/victo/WebProjects/Hacker-Portfolio/assets/functions/tetrisGame/tetrisGame.js:6:1`
`if (!document.getElementById("tetris-style")) {`
And `pongGame.js` has the exact same top-level check without guarding against SSR / non-browser!
Because `document` is accessed at the top level of `tetrisGame.js` and `pongGame.js` (and maybe `minesweeperGame.js`? Wait, `minesweeperGame.js` didn't throw because it doesn't have that check at top-level), when `tetrisGame.js` is imported, it immediately throws a `ReferenceError: document is not defined`!
That halts the execution of module loading in `main.js`, which prevents `tetrisGame.js`, `pongGame.js`, and anything imported after them (or causes JS execution to fail completely in `main.js`), so Snake (which is first or loaded differently) might be the only one that loaded successfully or `snake` was handled before `tetris` threw!

That is the absolute root cause! Top-level `document` access without `typeof document !== "undefined"` guard in `tetrisGame.js` and `pongGame.js`.
Let's guard the document/style injection in `tetrisGame.js` and `pongGame.js`:
```javascript
if (typeof document !== "undefined" && !document.getElementById("tetris-style")) {
  const link = document.createElement("link");
  link.id = "tetris-style";
  link.rel = "stylesheet";
  link.href = "assets/functions/tetrisGame/tetrisGame.css";
  document.head.appendChild(link);
}
```
and similarly in `pongGame.js`:
```javascript
if (typeof document !== "undefined" && !document.getElementById("pong-style")) {
  const link = document.createElement("link");
  link.id = "pong-style";
  link.rel = "stylesheet";
  link.href = "assets/functions/pongGame/pongGame.css";
  document.head.appendChild(link);
}
```

That is such an incredible catch! Top-level `document` references in ESM modules will throw instantly if evaluated in an environment where `document` isn't globally present or during module parsing/loading.

Let's fix `tetrisGame.js` and `pongGame.js` immediately.
Let's check `tetrisGame.js` lines 1 to 15.

